# RULE 17 — NO GUARD HOT-FILE THRASH (2026-07-17)

**Root cause of the serialize treadmill:** every PR edited `package.json` and/or `.github/workflows/locked-guards.yml` / `ci.yml` to wire a new `verify:*` script. Each merge conflicted every other open PR. Hours burned; almost no product progress.

## Law (non-negotiable)

When adding a new guard:

1. Add `scripts/verify-<name>.mjs`
2. Add `scripts/verify-steps/<NNN>-verify-<name>.mjs` that `export default { name, run(ctx) { … } }` and runs the guard via `ctx.run("node", ["scripts/verify-<name>.mjs"])`
3. **Do NOT** edit `package.json`, `.github/workflows/locked-guards.yml`, or `.github/workflows/ci.yml`
4. **Do NOT** edit `scripts/verify-steps/CLAIMED-NUMBERS.json` in feature PRs — the `NNNN-*.mjs` **filename is the claim** (TOOL-F03). Cursor = EVEN · Claude = ODD (`verify-verify-step-lane-band`). GitHub cannot run `merge=json-union`, so CLAIMED edits are a guaranteed conflict treadmill.

`verify:pre-commit` auto-discovers verify-steps. `verify-guard-wired` treats CI-via-steps as fully wired; package.json is optional local convenience only.

## CI enforcement

`scripts/verify-no-guard-hotfile-thrash.mjs` (via verify-steps) **fails** any PR that adds a new `verify:*` key to `package.json` or adds new guard `npm run` / `node scripts/verify-*.mjs` lines to locked-guards/ci vs `origin/main`.

## Drain tool

`scripts/ops/serialize-drain-open-prs.py` — detox hot files to main, then merge one real-green PR at a time. Prefer this over fragile shell loops.

